## Why This Is Asked
Tests for offline-first behavior are core for reliability but beginners often struggle with storage APIs and network conditions. This question isolates those concepts in a tangible, front-end context.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first strategy
- IndexedDB usage
- Sync mechanics and idempotence
- Conflict resolution policy
- CI network condition emulation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Cypress skeleton for offline caching test
describe('Offline-first sync', () => {
  it('caches submissions offline and syncs when online', () => {
    cy.visit('/form');
    cy.window().then(w => { w.navigator.onLine = false; });
    cy.get('#name').type('Alice');
    cy.get('#email').type('a@example.com');
    cy.get('#submit').click();
    // verify IndexedDB contains 1 entry
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt tests for different storage backends (IndexedDB vs LocalStorage)?
- How would you measure flakiness and improve CI stability?

## Why This Is Asked

Webhooks are central to reliable integrations in payments; testing ensures resilience to retries, dedup, and partial failures, which beginner testers can demonstrate through practical CI plans.

## Key Concepts

- At-least-once delivery
- Idempotency
- Retry strategies and jitter
- End-to-end testing with mocks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test: webhook sink with idempotency key check
const deliveries = new Map();
function deliver(ctx) {
  const key = ctx.idempotencyKey;
  if (deliveries.has(key)) return 'duplicate';
  deliveries.set(key, true);
  return 'delivered';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test out-of-order deliveries?
- How would you simulate a non-idempotent endpoint handle correctly?
